## 0.14.0
### Fixed
- fix(export): an overview stopped part-way (fewer tiles in its last planes)
  failed to export ("all input arrays must have the same shape"); all planes
  of a tiled overview now share one canvas.
- fix(export): brightfield images are placed by the middle of the image, not
  by the laser target. A target puts the laser on a point, and the laser sits
  where its marker was set in the camera image (13 - 57 um from the middle in
  these files); only the overview engine moved its targets by that shift.
  - The images taken in the Fluorescence tab (`FL_BMrep<N>`, also the
    combined ones) were 0.15 - 0.25 mm, with relative grid coordinates several
    mm, away from the overviews: BrillouinAcquisition
    stores their position in the grid frame in force when they were taken,
    before Start. They are now placed from `stage_position_raw` minus the
    image centre shift (`Payload.get_image_centre_raw()`), in the frame of
    the Brillouin repetition they are filed under
    (`Payload.raw_to_grid_frame()`: minus the absolute origin of the grid, or
    the raw position with relative coordinates).
  - Overview images from before the engine and per-point images are placed
    by their target minus the shift (`Payload.get_image_centre_shift()`).
  - `tools/add_image_centres.py` writes `image_centre_shift`,
    `fov_compensation` and (images taken by hand) `stage_position_raw` into
    files from before BrillouinAcquisition wrote them, from the scale
    calibration of each image's repetition and its camera ROI. Checked: FL images and overviews of old files register
    within 3 - 5 um, engine files 4 - 12 um.
### Removed
- Legacy code, after the files were converted: `tools/migrate_legacy_overviews.py`
  rewrites the attributes of the overview images of files from before the
  overview engine (channel, event, tile and stack index, repetition, position;
  no spectrum or image is touched), so the
  overview export has one reader: the old path that guessed events, tiles and
  repetition from the order and positions of the images
  (`Payload.has_overview_brightfield()`, `get_overview_brightfield_positions()`
  and their `Session` counterparts, `positions-overview-brightfield-*`) is
  gone. Images of the overview channels without the attributes are reported
  and not exported.
- Support of H5BM files before v0.0.4 (they raise `BadFileException`).
### Added
- feat(file): overview engine of BrillouinAcquisition (channel
  `Brightfield overview`): `OVERVIEW_EVENT_CHANNEL`,
  `OVERVIEW_CHANNELS`, `MeasurementData.get_overview_info()` (event, kind,
  tile and stack index, the image's own scale calibration, drift offset,
  FOV compensation and image centre shift, and the `anchor`: the CSV
  position in the middle of the image - the target the engine stores is
  not it), `Payload.get_overview_events()` (per event: objectives, drift
  decision, step, total, grid offset after, correlation),
  `get_overview_objectives()`, `get_surface_rescans()`,
  `get_resume_events()` and `Repetition.acquisition_state`.
- feat(export): the overview engine's images are exported like the z
  overviews, `Plots/Overview_BMrep<N>/overview_<n>_<time>.tif` (one file per
  event and objective, a z stack as multi-page TIFF) with a transform matrix
  per file that maps the CSV x, y onto its pixels - from the image's own
  calibration (the repetition's is that of the measuring objective: the
  `BrightfieldOverview_*` files exported through the Fluorescence export
  before had the wrong scale and a position off by the image centre shift)
  and the anchor - and an `overview_events.csv` per folder with what each
  file is. They are no longer also exported as
  `FL_BMrep<N>/BrightfieldOverview_*`.
- feat(export): drift correction while measuring. `Payload.get_runtime_drift()`,
  `get_point_drift_offsets()` (the offset every point was measured with,
  laid out like the grid) and `get_scan_plan()` (the order the points were
  measured in). The Brillouin CSV header gets `#drift_runtime_applied`,
  `..._applied_events`, `..._evaluated_events`, `..._max_offset_um`,
  `..._decisions`, `#acquisition_state` and the new overview/drift settings.
  `Export/*_BMrep<N>_runtime_drift.csv` has one line per drift step
  (decision, step, total, grid offset after, correlation, tiles compared and
  used, seconds since the reference, ...); the data CSV keeps the planned
  positions, which are the positions on the sample for every applied step.
  There is no second copy of the data with the points moved.
- feat(export): the grid definition in the CSV header (`#grid_<axis>_steps`,
  `_min_um`, `_max_um`, `_step_um`, `#grid_absolute_origin_<axis>_um`,
  `#grid_scan_loop_level_<axis>`, `#grid_coordinates_absolute`, the ROI
  polygons) from `Payload.get_grid_definition()`.
- `Session.get_overview_brightfield_keys()` also returns the images of the
  overview engine.
- feat(evaluation): second Brillouin shift quantity,
  `brillouin_shift_f_stokes_anti_stokes`, computed from the distance
  between the Stokes and Anti-Stokes Brillouin peaks instead of relative
  to the Rayleigh peak, corrected for the VIPA spectrum's free spectral
  range (FSR, taken from the calibration fit - not this frame's own
  Rayleigh peaks) - only defined when exactly 2 Brillouin regions are
  selected and a calibration is available. Kept alongside the existing
  Rayleigh-referenced `brillouin_shift_f`, for both the main evaluation
  grid and background points.
- feat(session): derived values (`brillouin_shift_f` and friends) are now
  recomputed from already-stored peak fits when a session file is
  loaded, so a previously-evaluated repetition picks up new/changed
  derived quantities without re-fitting.
- feat(evaluation): `EvaluationModel.evaluation_mode` ('single', the
  default, or 'sum') - in 'sum' mode, camera frame repeats at each point
  are additionally interpolated onto a common frequency axis, summed,
  and fit once, and that single sum-fit becomes the reported value for
  every fit-derived quantity, instead of averaging the separately-fit
  per-frame values - while still fitting every frame separately
  underneath, so `brillouin_shift_frame_spread`/
  `rayleigh_shift_frame_spread` and the other quality diagnostics keep
  working unchanged.
- feat(evaluation): `EvaluationController.get_fits_combined()` and
  `get_combined_spectrum()`, for viewers (e.g. BMicro's per-pixel
  spectrum dialog) to show the 'sum'-mode combined fit/spectrum for a
  point alongside its per-frame fits/spectra.
- feat(session): support BrillouinAcquisition's adaptive frame extension
  - a per-point HDF5 dataset carrying a `frames_actual` attribute smaller
    than its own frame-count dimension (padded to accommodate a variable
    number of extra low-signal frames) now has its trailing, unused
    padded slots trimmed off in `MeasurementData.get_image()`/
    `get_image_count()` (`bmlab/file.py`), before any evaluation code
    (`ImageController.extract_spectra()` and everything derived from
    `len(imgs)`) ever sees the array. Files without the attribute
    (written before this feature, or with it unused) are read exactly
    as before.

## 0.13.0 - 2026-09-10
### Added
- feat(evaluation): fit-quality diagnostics (SNR, NRMSE, peak-center
  uncertainty) and frame-to-frame reproducibility, with configurable
  pass/fail thresholds (`EvaluationModel.quality_thresholds`,
  `get_default_quality_thresholds()`)
- feat(export): combine all Brillouin parameters into one CSV per
  repetition, with repetition selection and applied quality-threshold
  metadata
- feat(export): stage-to-overview-image transform matrix export

### Fixed
- fix(evaluation): allocate `brillouin_shift_frame_spread`/
  `rayleigh_shift_frame_spread` results arrays on init, so a default
  threshold on them doesn't crash before the first evaluation
- fix(evaluation): remove unused legacy `brillouin_snr` derived value

